WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:16.215
Unit twenty-three: Nature and Parks. Today you will give advice about enjoying and protecting nature.

4
00:00:16.515 --> 00:00:19.295
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:23.397
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.077
Nature.

7
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:29.348
Nature means plants, animals and the world not made by people.

8
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.566
I feel calm in nature.

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.210
Your turn. Say: Nature.

10
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:37.998
Nature.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.472
Park.

12
00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:43.296
Park means a public area with grass and trees.

13
00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:45.627
We have picnics in the park.

14
00:00:46.217 --> 00:00:48.695
Your turn. Say: Park.

15
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:52.233
Park.

16
00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:53.659
Tree.

17
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.276
Tree means a tall plant with a trunk and leaves.

18
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:59.686
We planted a mango tree.

19
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:02.286
Your turn. Say: Tree.

20
00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:05.879
Tree.

21
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:07.444
Bird.

22
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.274
Bird means an animal with wings and feathers.

23
00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:13.674
I can hear a bird singing.

24
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:17.005
Your turn. Say: Bird.

25
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:20.775
Bird.

26
00:01:21.517 --> 00:01:22.436
Fresh air.

27
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.775
Fresh air means clean air outside.

28
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:28.476
Let's go out for some fresh air.

29
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:31.503
Your turn. Say: Fresh air.

30
00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.472
Fresh air.

31
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:36.974
Walk.

32
00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:40.076
Walk means a short trip on foot.

33
00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:42.520
We go for a walk after dinner.

34
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:45.699
Your turn. Say: Walk.

35
00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:49.337
Walk.

36
00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:51.015
Protect.

37
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:54.492
Protect means to keep something safe from harm.

38
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:56.967
We must protect our forests.

39
00:01:57.583 --> 00:02:00.143
Your turn. Say: Protect.

40
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:03.780
Protect.

41
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:05.471
Relax.

42
00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:08.854
Relax means to rest and feel calm.

43
00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.206
Nature helps me relax.

44
00:02:11.817 --> 00:02:14.875
Your turn. Say: Relax.

45
00:02:17.733 --> 00:02:18.827
Relax.

46
00:02:19.633 --> 00:02:23.087
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.565
Visal, do you like spending time in nature?

48
00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:31.243
Yes! I go for a walk in the park every Sunday.

49
00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.384
What should visitors do in the park?

50
00:02:35.483 --> 00:02:37.181
We should take our rubbish home.

51
00:02:38.283 --> 00:02:39.691
And what shouldn't we do?

52
00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:43.979
We shouldn't pick the flowers or disturb the birds.

53
00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.401
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.876
Grammar focus: Should and shouldn't.

55
00:02:50.176 --> 00:02:51.352
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.655
We should protect parks.

57
00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.074
We shouldn't leave rubbish.

58
00:02:56.983 --> 00:02:58.635
We should plant more trees.

59
00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:02.668
Use 'should' for good ideas and 'shouldn't' for bad ideas.

60
00:03:03.417 --> 00:03:06.893
Be careful! Don't say: We shouldn't to leave rubbish.

61
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:11.216
Say: We shouldn't leave rubbish.

62
00:03:11.516 --> 00:03:13.156
Don't use 'to' after 'shouldn't'.

63
00:03:13.967 --> 00:03:16.642
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:17.433 --> 00:03:18.620
Time in Nature.

65
00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.338
Spending time in nature helps us relax.

66
00:03:22.333 --> 00:03:25.656
In the park, we can walk under the trees and listen to the birds.

67
00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.316
The fresh air is good for our body and mind.

68
00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.729
We should protect these places for the future.

69
00:03:33.733 --> 00:03:36.255
We shouldn't leave rubbish or damage the trees.

70
00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:41.229
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:43.967
We blank leave rubbish in the park.

72
00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:47.433
A, shouldn't. B, should. C, should to.

73
00:03:50.967 --> 00:03:53.094
The answer is A: shouldn't.

74
00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.737
To keep something safe from harm is to blank.

75
00:03:57.037 --> 00:04:00.737
A, protect. B, relax. C, walk.

76
00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.241
The answer is A: protect.

77
00:04:07.383 --> 00:04:09.267
Clean air outside is blank.

78
00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:13.267
A, fresh air. B, nature. C, a park.

79
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.858
The answer is A: fresh air.

80
00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:23.067
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:23.917 --> 00:04:26.276
Why is it good to spend time in nature?

82
00:04:35.083 --> 00:04:36.526
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:36.826 --> 00:04:45.538
Spending time in nature helps me relax, and the fresh air is healthy. We should protect parks, and we shouldn't leave rubbish.

84
00:04:45.838 --> 00:04:47.664
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:52.526
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and should and shouldn't.

86
00:04:52.826 --> 00:04:57.289
Today's value is respect for nature. Protect animals, trees and rivers.

87
00:04:57.589 --> 00:05:00.555
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

88
00:05:00.855 --> 00:05:03.577
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

